        { type: 'p', text: "As you've grown older, your social environment has expanded to include neighbors, schoolmates, teachers, and others in your community. You've probably heard a lot about peer pressure — today the word peers usually means your friends or a larger group of people your own age. The friends you choose can have an important effect on your level of wellness: friends who practice unhealthful behaviors can pressure you to do the same, and it's sometimes hard to stand up to that. Choosing friends who favor healthful habits makes it easier for you to choose wellness too." }
