        { type: 'p', text: "With that much control over your own life comes responsibility. Begin by learning the answers to two questions: what are the leading causes of death among teenagers today, and what risk behaviors are associated with those deaths? The three most common causes of teenage death — accidents, suicide, and homicide — are not illnesses at all, and there is a risk behavior common to all three: substance abuse, the use of alcohol or drugs. Nearly half of all car accidents involve alcohol or drugs, and many suicides and homicides are tied to substance abuse as well, since impaired judgment under the influence can lead to violent or reckless behavior." }
